# tally 2.2.1 (#219, 219.1), L §6.1 and §5.19: a read of the movement away from the places that book it is
# HOLE-SAME, naming both rows, for an observed row stated same as a planned instance too: in1 and in2 disagree on the
# amount of cash (100.00 and 120.00 PLN). tally 2.2 tested only two observed rows (the review's s5/hs_disagree.tally).
=== hs.tally
model hs
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place wallet: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input d1: date
input a1: money PLN
input a2: money PLN

move in1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a1
move in2: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to wallet amount a2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  a1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  a2 = 120.00 PLN "s"
  opening[wallet] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version later
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-05-01
  same in1 = in2

ask today: bal(wallet, 2026-03-31)
ask before: bal(wallet, 2026-03-31) as known 2026-04-01
ask amt: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask f: flows(wallet, 2026-03)
=== expect amt
amt: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but leg cash differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 120.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2)
  unfulfilled: in1
  unfulfilled: in2
  cut 2026-06-10
